From 66a1077958cc71263d8a9327436211893298bb83 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 09:07:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] feat(od-sevev): redraw the Jerusalem-stone plaza and lane
 with short mortar joints

Manual test A1: the plaza read as worms. The 1-px ink press cable meandered down
the 128x96 plaza tile and lined up across copies into snakes, and the lane's
cable was the black wavy line above the ticker. One tone in a 32-px running bond
with full-length pale seams read as a brick wall.

wave5.Paving lays one floor per era for the lane and the plaza: slabs of random
length in 2-3 stone tones, course heights 10/12/14, joints kept 5 px apart from
the courses above and below, 1-px mortar one value step off the stone (never
black) in one-slab runs with gaps, chisel flecks, lit worn edges, square big
stones and two far-apart cement repairs. No cable. Plaza 192x192, lane 192x28
(the lane's last course runs on in the plaza's rows 0-4). All floor details
are 3:1 or less against the stone; every slab tone keeps 4.5:1 against the
Suitcase outline and 3:1 against its maroon (asserted).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UJWVH11egMQ4r4GfyoMb4p
