From 7fca710888b185ae292c4b1da0a936a3521a6ea1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 09:09:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] feat(od-sevev): draw the picker booth as a kraft
 cardboard folding screen

Manual test B13: booth_frame read as a thin brown line. At x4 its off-white
wings were 12-16 logical px and the transparent opening let the dimmed stage
show between the tiles.

Same size, 9-slice [6, 10, 6, 4] and content box (the view's BOOTH_TOP / SIDE /
BOTTOM insets are unchanged). It is now drawn as a tabletop folding screen in
kraft cardboard: the back panel carries a blank flag-blue printed band, the two
unprinted side wings stand 2 rows lower (the left one lit, the right one in
shade, a crease at each fold), the back panel's face is opaque behind the grid
(so the tile gaps show cardboard), and there is a shelf. The tile outline is
7.5:1 on it. booth_frame_tall shares the drawing (wave8.booth_art). Blank: no
text, emblem, ballot letters, party colour or flag stripes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UJWVH11egMQ4r4GfyoMb4p
